<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Bhor State</h1><p class="st-meta">1697 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Bhor</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maratha state in the Sahyadri hills south of Pune, ruled by the hereditary Pant Sachiv ministers of the Maratha court.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bhor was granted in 1697 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shankaraji-narayan">Shankaraji Narayan</a>, appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv">Sachiv</a> (minister) by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaram-i">Rajaram</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deshastha-brahmin">Deshastha Brahmin</a> family held the office of Pant Sachiv and the lands that supported it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv">Pant Sachivs</a> ruled a hilly territory of forts and small farms along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohida-fort">Rohida</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajgad">Rajgad</a>. After 1818 they came under British protection and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>. The state introduced some representative institutions before independence.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Bhor merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> in 1960, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bhor-state.jpg" alt="Bhor State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhor_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1697 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bhor</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shankaraji Narayan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bhor</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=bhor-state" aria-label="Bhor State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6682 1504 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bhor State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7002 1760L6991 1757M7002 1760L7364 1601M7002 1760L7364 1602M7002 1760L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7002 1760h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7002 1760h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=bhor-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
